CONCERNING
PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN
FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF NORTH GORONTALO
Considering: a. that in order to protect the constitutional rights of women and children in accordance with the mandate of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia, the Government of North Gorontalo Regency is jointly responsible in the implementation of protection of women and children against acts of violence.
b. that North Gorontalo Regency which has the Philosophy of Adat Bersendi Syara, Syara Bersendi Kitabullah, upholds Religious Values and Customs as well as noble Character, the Government of North Gorontalo Regency is morally fully responsible for the protection of women and children from acts of violence.
c. that every citizen has the right to be free from torture or treatment that degrades dignity, self-worth and human dignity and has the right to obtain a sense of security and freedom from all forms of violence
d. that the increase in violent treatment against women and children in North Gorontalo Regency is an act that degrades human dignity, so that the role of the North Gorontalo Regency government is required so that women and children are protected from acts of violence
e. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women and Children Against Acts of Violence
In View of: 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
3. Law Number 38 of 2000 concerning Establishment of Gorontalo Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2000 Number 182, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4010);
4. Law Number 11 of 2007 concerning the establishment of North Gorontalo Regency;
5. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606);
6. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
7. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
8. Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning Formation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);
9. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);
10. Government Regulation Number 38 of 2007 concerning Division of Government Affairs between the Government, Provincial Regional Government, and Regency/City Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 437);
11. Government Regulation Number 9 of 2008 concerning Procedures and Mechanisms for Integrated Services for Witnesses and/or Victims of Criminal Acts of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 22, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4818);
12. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for Implementation of Women's Protection;
13. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 3 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for Implementation of Child Protection;
14. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards for Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence;
15. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 concerning Guidelines for Establishment and Development of Integrated Service Centers;
16. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for Handling Child Victims of Violence;
17. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 19 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for Empowerment of Women Victims of Violence;
18. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 80 of 2015 concerning Formation of Regional Legal Products;
With Mutual Agreement

Article 18
(1) The Regional Government in conducting cooperation and coordination for the Protection of Women and Children from acts of violence, shall establish FP2ATK;
(2) The membership of FP2ATK consists of elements of:
a. regional government;
b. vertical agencies;
c. educational institutions; and
d. community organizations that care about the protection of women and children from acts of violence.
(3) The Organizational Structure of FP2ATK as referred to in paragraph (2) consists of:
a. policy formulation working group;
b. socialization working group;
c. service working group; and
d. data, information, monitoring and evaluation working group.
(4) The establishment and term of office of FP2ATK members as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be stipulated by Regent's Decree.

Article 12
(1) Regional Government implements integrated services for victims of acts of violence as referred to in Article 5 letter b through activities:
a. complaint services;
b. health services;
c. counseling;
d. spiritual guidance;
e. social rehabilitation services;
f. legal aid and assistance services; and/or g. repatriation and reintegration.
(2) Services as referred to in paragraph (1) must be supported with facilities in the form of:
a. special service rooms in police lines;
b. expert and professional personnel;
c. service centers and safe houses; and/or
d. other facilities and infrastructure needed for victim recovery.
(3) Implementation of services for victims of acts of violence is carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government together with P2TP2A with other social institutions;
(4) P2TP2A and other social institutions as referred to in paragraph (3) may receive and send case referrals from other service units in a networked manner;
(5) Integrated services for victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) through paragraph (4) are implemented in accordance with standard operating procedures;
(6) Provisions regarding Standard Operating Procedures as referred to in paragraph (5) are regulated by Governor Regulation.

Article 22
(1) The Regional Government in the context of providing services to victims of acts of violence, establishes P2TP2A;
(2) P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) has the duties to:
a. provide services, including:
1. receive complaints/reports of violence against women and/or children, consultation, and counseling;
2. receive and send case referrals from Regency/City Regional Government or institutions established by the Regency/City Regional Government;
3. provide legal assistance and support;
4. health;
5. social rehabilitation;
6. legal services; and
7. repatriation and social reintegration.
b. provide protection to victims of acts of violence, reporters and witnesses.
(3) The appointment of P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be stipulated by Regent's Decree.
(4) Regional Apparatus shall provide guidance to P2TP2A in carrying out duties as referred to in paragraph (2).

Article 23
(1) In certain circumstances the Regional Government may conduct cooperation with:
a. other regional governments;
b. police;
c. advocates;
d. health workers;
e. social workers;
f. volunteer assistants;
g. spiritual counselors;
h. other law enforcers, to assist victims in the court hearing process;
i. national commission on violence against women;
j. Indonesian child protection commission or Child Protection Institution; and/or
k. certain parties as desired for the benefit of victims.
(2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) may take the form of:
a. socialization;
b. provision of legal aid;
c. health services;
d. victim assistance;
e. counseling;
f. social rehabilitation;
g. spiritual guidance; and/or
h. repatriation and social reintegration.

Article 14
(1) Protection of children who are victims of acts of violence as referred to in article 6 letter a shall be the responsibility of the Regional Government;
(2) Protection of children victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by:
a. formulating policies for prevention, risk reduction for vulnerable groups, handling of victims and data and information systems for children;
b. providing maintenance, care, and social rehabilitation for neglected children, both within institutions and outside institutions;
c. providing shelters, maintenance and care for neglected children; and providing special protection to children.
Article 15
(1) Provisions regarding prevention and services for acts of violence in the protection of women as referred to in Article 7 through Article 13 shall apply mutatis mutandis to the protection of children from acts of violence;
(2) In addition to carrying out prevention as referred to in paragraph (1), also by way of increasing family capacity in child protection and child-rearing skills.
